    "html": "<p>Correct answer: B</p>\n<p>A: Note: Student calculated the area as a rectangle (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\times 10\"></span>) instead of a triangle.</p>\n<p>B: Note: Area under the graph = <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\text{ s} \\times 6.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{ A} = 0.030 \\text{ C}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>C: Note: Student calculated the triangle area but failed to convert mA to A (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.5 \\times 10 \\times 6 = 30\"></span>).</p>\n<p>D: Note: Student calculated the rectangle area and failed to convert mA to A (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10 \\times 6 = 60\"></span>).</p>"
